[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: KM271-WiFi System Requirements
UID: KM271-SYS
VERSION: 0.1
OPTIONS:
  VIEW_STYLE: Table

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document lists the system level requirements of the KM271-WiFi, a
WiFi enabled replacement for the Buderus KM271 communication module of
Logamatic heating controllers. The requirements describe what the complete
product (board, mechanics and firmware) has to achieve, independent of the
chosen implementation.

Scope: hardware revision v2.0 (ESP32-S3, step-down converter, USB with
selectable data path). Optional extensions (e.g. the W5500 Ethernet
extension) have their own requirement sets that trace to this document.

Conventions: "shall" = mandatory, "should" = recommended, "may" = optional.
STATUS gives the review state of the requirement, COMPLIANCE the state of
the current design against it.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose and integration

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-001
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Drop-in replacement for the KM271
STATEMENT: >>>
The KM271-WiFi shall be insertable into the KM271 slot of a Buderus Logamatic 2107 (and compatible HS 2105) controller in place of the original Buderus KM271 module, without modification of the controller.
<<<
SOURCE: README.md, DOC/Hardware Description.md

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-002
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Read heating data
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall read the operating values, states and error messages that the Logamatic provides on its KM271 service interface.
<<<
SOURCE: dewenni/ESP_Buderus_KM271, the78mole/ESPhome-KM271-WiFi

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-003
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Change supported parameters
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow changing those Logamatic parameters that the KM271 interface supports for writing (e.g. operating modes, set points, hot water settings).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-004
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Wireless network connectivity
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall connect to an IEEE 802.11 b/g/n network in the 2.4 GHz band.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-005
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Optional wired network connectivity
STATEMENT: >>>
The system should support wired Ethernet through an optional plug-on extension, for installations without usable WiFi coverage (e.g. concrete basements).
<<<
SOURCE: EXTENSIONS/ETH_W5500/README.md

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-006
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Smart home integration
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the heating data and the writable parameters available to home automation systems (at least Home Assistant) via a documented network protocol (e.g. MQTT or the ESPHome native API).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-007
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Partially met
TITLE: Exchangeable firmware
STATEMENT: >>>
The hardware shall support different, independently developed firmware implementations (currently ESPHome-KM271-WiFi and ESP_Buderus_KM271) without hardware modification.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The community uses two firmware projects with different integration concepts. The hardware must not lock users into one of them.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Both firmwares need an ESP32-S3 build and a board preset for v2.0, see KM271-SW-060.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Power supply

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-010
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Supply from the Logamatic
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall be operable from the 5 V supply of the KM271 slot alone, without any external power supply.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-011
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Robustness against a weak slot supply
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall operate without brown-out or reset at an effective source resistance of the Logamatic 5 V supply of at least 2 Ohm, including WiFi transmit current peaks.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Several Logamatic controllers have a weak 5 V rail (LM317 on the NM 282 power board); users of older boards reported brown-outs.
<<<
SOURCE: >>>
DOC/Power-Analysis/README.md (Buck regulates up to ~2.25 Ohm at a 460 mA step)
<<<
COMMENT: Value of the real source resistance is not measured yet.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-012
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Performance
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Low load on the slot supply
STATEMENT: >>>
The system should draw as little current as possible from the Logamatic. The peak current drawn from the slot shall not exceed 400 mA without extensions.
<<<
SOURCE: DOC/Power-Analysis/README.md (386 mA at the ESP32-S3 worst case)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-013
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Alternative supply via USB
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall be operable from a USB host or USB power supply, alone or in parallel to the Logamatic supply, without feeding current from one source into the other.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Local inputs, outputs and extensions

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-020
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Simulation, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Exhaust gas temperature sensor
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide the connection and conditioning for the Buderus exhaust gas temperature sensor (FG, NTC about 100 kOhm at 25 degC) towards the Logamatic, like the original KM271, over the full setting range of the exhaust gas threshold (50 to 250 degC).
<<<
SOURCE: DOC/Abgassensor/README.md

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-021
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Inspection, Test
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Additional sensors
STATEMENT: >>>
The system should provide inputs for additional local sensors: a OneWire bus, analog inputs for NTC sensors and a pulse input for an oil meter.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-022
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Interface
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Extension interface
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide an extension interface with power, SPI and I2C for plug-on modules (e.g. Ethernet, display).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-023
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Status indication
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall indicate its basic operating states (network, activity, communication with the Logamatic, errors) by LEDs visible on the module.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-024
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Local user controls
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall provide a reset and a boot button and may provide additional user buttons.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Commissioning and maintenance

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-030
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Flashing without external programmer
STATEMENT: >>>
Firmware shall be flashable over the on-board USB connector without an external programmer and without pressing buttons.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-031
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Recovery flashing path
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall offer a flashing path that works even if the firmware has disabled or broken the native USB interface of the microcontroller.
<<<
COMMENT: Realized as assembly option (CP2102N data path, see KM271-HW-034).

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-032
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Update over the network
STATEMENT: The firmware shall be updatable over the network (OTA) once installed.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-033
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Usability
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Demonstration
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: First-time setup without tools
STATEMENT: >>>
A user shall be able to configure network access of a fresh device with a smartphone or PC only, without installing software.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Environment, safety and mechanics

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-040
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Mechanical
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Mechanical fit in the slot
STATEMENT: >>>
The module shall fit the KM271 slot including its guide rails and the space between neighbouring modules and the housing.
<<<
SOURCE: MECH/, project memory (guide rail clearance)

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-041
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Environmental
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Analysis
COMPLIANCE: Not verified
TITLE: Operating environment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall operate in the ambient conditions inside a Logamatic control housing mounted on a boiler: 0 to 60 degC, non-condensing.
<<<
COMMENT: Temperature range is an assumption and needs confirmation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-042
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: EMC
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Review, Test
COMPLIANCE: Partially met
TITLE: Electromagnetic compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall not disturb the operation of the Logamatic or of other modules in the controller, and shall withstand electrostatic discharge on user accessible connectors.
<<<
SOURCE: EMC layout review 2026-11-24
COMMENT: Layout reviewed rule based; no EMC measurement yet.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-043
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Protection
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Safety extra-low voltage only
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall only connect to safety extra-low voltage circuits of the Logamatic and shall not be connected to mains voltage.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Production and licensing

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-050
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Manufacturing
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Assembly by a PCB service
STATEMENT: >>>
The board shall be producible and SMT assembled by JLCPCB with parts available from LCSC. Through-hole parts shall be optional and may be fitted by the buyer.
<<<
SOURCE: KM217-WiFi/jlc-sourcing.md

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-052
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Should
VERIFICATION: Analysis
COMPLIANCE: Not verified
TITLE: Sales price target
STATEMENT: >>>
The KM271-WiFi should be sellable for less than 50 USD per unit, based on a
production order of 100 boards at JLCPCB (PCB, parts and assembly).
<<<
SOURCE: Maulwurf, 2026-11-25
COMMENT: >>>
No cost calculation for the v2.0 board at 100 pcs yet. Optional extensions
(e.g. ETH-W5500, see ETH-SYS-031) are not included.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: KM271-SYS-051
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Constraint
PRIORITY: Must
VERIFICATION: Inspection
COMPLIANCE: Met
TITLE: Open hardware
STATEMENT: >>>
Hardware design files and documentation shall be published under the TAPR Open Hardware License v1.0.
<<<
SOURCE: LICENSE

[[/SECTION]]
